WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.441
As environments grow more complex, detection engineering becomes increasingly important.

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:07.913
Organizations need maintainable detections, reliable telemetry, strong documentation,

00:00:07.913 --> 00:00:10.084
meaningful metrics, and effective collaboration.

00:00:10.084 --> 00:00:13.990
Cloud services, SaaS platforms, identity systems, endpoint tooling, applications,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.595
and data pipelines all change quickly.

00:00:16.595 --> 00:00:21.369
Detection programs must adapt without losing control of quality or ownership.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:27.012
The future of detection engineering is not just more alerts or more tools.

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:30.919
It is better visibility, clearer context, stronger lifecycle management,

00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:34.391
and more disciplined improvement based on operational evidence.

00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:40.468
Automation and AI can help with parts of the work, such as summarization, enrichment,

00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:42.639
review support, or test generation.

00:00:42.639 --> 00:00:46.979
Human judgment remains essential for understanding business context, investigation needs,

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:48.716
and acceptable operational tradeoffs.

00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:53.924
Detection engineering helps create sustainable defensive capabilities that evolve alongside changing threats,

00:00:53.924 --> 00:00:55.661
technologies, and business requirements.

00:00:55.661 --> 00:01:01.304
The organizations that benefit most will treat detection as a long-term engineering practice.

00:01:01.304 --> 00:01:06.512
Future programs will likely place more emphasis on detection portability, structured metadata,

00:01:06.512 --> 00:01:08.683
testable detection content, coverage mapping,

00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:13.023
and tighter connections between detection work and incident response lessons.

00:01:13.023 --> 00:01:18.232
They will also need stronger partnerships with data engineering and platform teams.

00:01:18.232 --> 00:01:23.441
As telemetry volume grows, detection engineers will need reliable pipelines, clear schemas,

00:01:23.441 --> 00:01:26.046
useful enrichment, and sustainable storage decisions.

00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:30.386
Detection engineering is the discipline of designing, building, maintaining, measuring,

00:01:30.386 --> 00:01:32.557
documenting, and improving security detections.

00:01:32.557 --> 00:01:38.634
It transforms telemetry into actionable defensive visibility and relies on collaboration across security teams.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:42.540
Mature programs use lifecycle management, testing, tuning, documentation, metrics,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.013
and continuous improvement to maintain effective defensive capabilities.

00:01:46.013 --> 00:01:49.051
Detection engineering is not simply writing alerts.

00:01:49.051 --> 00:01:54.260
It is the engineering practice of creating reliable visibility into security-relevant activity.
